{{!
    @template local_ai_course_assistant/analytics_tab_byunit

    By Unit tab of the analytics dashboard. Replaces the innerHTML string that
    amd/src/analytics_dashboard.js used to build for this pane
    (CONTRIB-10574 #278). Section names come from course data and are
    auto-escaped here instead of being hand-escaped in JavaScript.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * chartheight - pixel height for the bar chart canvas
    * str_section - column heading for the section name
    * str_active - column heading for active AI users
    * str_messages - column heading for the message count
    * str_permsg - column heading for messages per student
    * rows - one entry per section, each with section, students, messages
      and permsg

    Example context (json):
    {
        "chartheight": 80,
        "str_section": "Section",
        "str_active": "Active AI users",
        "str_messages": "Messages",
        "str_permsg": "Messages per student",
        "rows": [
            {"section": "Unit 1: Foundations", "students": "22", "messages": "140", "permsg": "6.4"}
        ]
    }
}}
<div class="row mb-4">
    <div class="col-12">
        <canvas id="sola-chart-byunit" height="{{chartheight}}"></canvas>
    </div>
</div>
<table class="table table-sm table-striped">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>{{str_section}}</th>
            <th>{{str_active}}</th>
            <th>{{str_messages}}</th>
            <th>{{str_permsg}}</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        {{#rows}}
            <tr>
                <td>{{section}}</td>
                <td>{{students}}</td>
                <td>{{messages}}</td>
                <td>{{permsg}}</td>
            </tr>
        {{/rows}}
    </tbody>
</table>
